diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0979c31
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy on one server
+
+Fizzy includes a Kamal configuration for a small, single-server installation.
+The server needs Linux, Docker, and SSH access for the user Kamal will use.
+Kamal Proxy obtains and renews the TLS certificate, so ports 80 and 443 must
+point at the server and the DNS record for the host must already exist.
+
+1. Copy the secrets template and edit `.kamal/secrets`:
+
+   ```sh
+   cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+   ```
+
+   Set `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`, `RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`,
+   `SMTP_USERNAME`, and `SMTP_PASSWORD`. `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` is the key for
+   the production credentials; generate the other application secret with
+   `bin/rails secret`.
+
+2. Edit `config/deploy.yml`, replacing `your-fizzy.example.com` in the web
+   host, proxy host, app host, SMTP domain, and sender address. Set the SMTP
+   server in `SMTP_ADDRESS`. Set `KAMAL_IMAGE`, `KAMAL_REGISTRY_SERVER`, and
+   `KAMAL_REGISTRY_USERNAME` if the image should be published somewhere other
+   than the defaults.
+
+3. Ensure the remote Docker user can be reached over SSH, then run:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+The deployment uses one web container. Puma loads the Solid Queue plugin, so
+background jobs run in the same container as the web process. The
+`fizzy_storage` Docker volume is mounted at `/rails/storage`; it contains the
+SQLite primary, cache, cable, and queue databases as well as local uploads and
+is deliberately retained across deploys.
+
+To deploy subsequent changes, run `bin/kamal deploy`. Use `bin/kamal app exec`
+for Rails commands, for example `bin/kamal app exec -i --reuse bin/rails db:migrate`.
